    "opt": true,
    "img": "i-roti"
   }
  ],
  "steps": [
   {
    "t": "Boil water in a pot. Add tea leaves tied in a small cloth.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-tea-1",
     "s-tea-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Put the paneer block into the boiling brown water. Leave it for about 10 minutes.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-soak-1",
     "s-soak-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Lift the paneer out with tongs.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-lift-1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Cut the paneer into triangle pieces.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-cut-1",
     "s-cut-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Heat oil in a kadai.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-oil-1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add cumin seeds, bay leaf, cinnamon, star anise and dry red chilli.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-spice-1",
     "s-spice-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add the crushed onion and cook, stirring.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-onion-1",
     "s-onion-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add chopped green chilli and stir.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-chilli-1",
     "s-chilli-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add red chilli powder, turmeric, coriander powder and salt.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-masala-1",
     "s-masala-2",
     "s-masala-3"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Cook, stirring, until the masala turns thick and dark.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-cook-1",
     "s-cook-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add a ladle of water and mix.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-water-1",
     "s-water-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add the tomato puree and cook, stirring.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-tomato-1",
     "s-tomato-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add another ladle of water.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-water-3"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Cover the kadai with a lid and cook.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-cover-1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Add the paneer pieces.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-paneer-1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Sprinkle kasuri methi on top.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-methi-1",
     "s-methi-2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Mix gently until the paneer is coated with masala.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-mix-1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "t": "Serve hot with roti.",
    "imgs": [
     "s-serve-1",
     "s-serve-2"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "tags": [
   "gas",
   "high-protein"
  ],
  "notes": "No amounts shown, all quantities guessed. Narration is garbled Hindi: tea leaves (chai patti) and the 10 minutes come from it; the white cloth bag dropped into the water is assumed to hold the tea leaves. The pale powder sprinkled in step 9 looks like salt (not named). The water added by ladle may be the brown soaking water. Cover-and-cook time and cooking time after the lid are not stated. The name kaleji (liver) is only the dish style: the paneer is just soaked to turn brown, no meat. Star anise is tagged whole-spices. Protein counts the paneer only."
 },
